findings.suggestion:
Use OR (`||`) to match the variable name and the convention in confirm.handler.ts:

  const isTeamAdminOrOwner =
    (await isTeamAdmin(user.id, booking.eventType?.teamId ?? 0)) ||
    (await isTeamOwner(user.id, booking.eventType?.teamId ?? 0));

Or, since `isTeamAdmin` already covers both ADMIN and OWNER roles, simply:

  const isTeamAdminOrOwner = !!(await isTeamAdmin(user.id, booking.eventType?.teamId ?? 0));

Also note: passing `teamId ?? 0` when eventType.teamId is null will look up membership for teamId=0 (never matching) - consider short-circuiting when there is no team.

