findings.suggestion:
Normalize the guest email to lowercase before the blacklist check, matching the existing convention. For example:
```ts
const uniqueGuests = guests.filter((guest) => {
  const guestEmail = guest.toLowerCase();
  return (
    !booking.attendees.some((attendee) => guestEmail === attendee.email.toLowerCase()) &&
    !blacklistedGuestEmails.includes(guestEmail)
  );
});
```
This makes the blacklist check case-insensitive, consistent with checkIfBookerEmailIsBlocked.ts and handleNewBooking.ts. Consider also lowercasing the attendee.email comparison for the same reason.

